{"content":[{"c":["MERCHANT"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["A person who buys and sells commodities for profit. The barter system of trade gave way in time to a system where professional merchants facilitated the exchange of goods. At first, it was for payment in silver pieces (",{"href":"?bref=Gen.23.16","r":"Gen.23.16","rawR":"Gen.23.16","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Gen.23.16","value":"Gen.23.16"}],"t":"ref","v":"Gn 23:16"},") and then in coinage or some other medium of exchange. Merchants operated locally and internationally with Arameans (",{"href":"?bref=1Kgs.20.34","r":"1Kgs.20.34","rawR":"1Kgs.20.34","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Kgs.20.34","value":"1Kgs.20.34"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Kgs 20:34"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Ezek.27.16-18","r":"Ezek.27.16-18","rawR":"Ezek.27.16-18","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ezek.27.16-18","value":"Ezek.27.16-18"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ez 27:16-18"},"), Canaanites and Phoenicians (",{"href":"?bref=Isa.23.2,8","r":"Isa.23.2,8","rawR":"Isa.23.2,8","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Isa.23.2,8","value":"Isa.23.2,8"}],"t":"ref","v":"Is 23:2, 8"},"), Assyrians (",{"href":"?bref=Nah.3.16","r":"Nah.3.16","rawR":"Nah.3.16","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Nah.3.16","value":"Nah.3.16"}],"t":"ref","v":"Na 3:16"},"), Babylonians, Persians, Greeks, and Romans. Some merchants traveled afar (",{"href":"?bref=Neh.13.16-20","r":"Neh.13.16-20","rawR":"Neh.13.16-20","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Neh.13.16-20","value":"Neh.13.16-20"}],"t":"ref","v":"Neh 13:16-20"},"). Desert peoples with caravans traded their wares in many lands (",{"href":"?bref=Ezek.27.15,20-23","r":"Ezek.27.15,20-23","rawR":"Ezek.27.15,20-23","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ezek.27.15,20-23","value":"Ezek.27.15,20-23"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ez 27:15, 20-23"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Ezek.38.13","r":"Ezek.38.13","rawR":"Ezek.38.13","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ezek.38.13","value":"Ezek.38.13"}],"t":"ref","v":"38:13"},"). They operated in bazaars and set up shops for trade (",{"href":"?bref=1Kgs.20.34","r":"1Kgs.20.34","rawR":"1Kgs.20.34","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Kgs.20.34","value":"1Kgs.20.34"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Kgs 20:34"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Neh.3.31","r":"Neh.3.31","rawR":"Neh.3.31","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Neh.3.31","value":"Neh.3.31"}],"t":"ref","v":"Neh 3:31"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Neh.13.19-20","r":"Neh.13.19-20","rawR":"Neh.13.19-20","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Neh.13.19-20","value":"Neh.13.19-20"}],"t":"ref","v":"13:19-20"},"). Commodities were held in storehouses (",{"href":"?bref=Gen.41.49","r":"Gen.41.49","rawR":"Gen.41.49","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Gen.41.49","value":"Gen.41.49"}],"t":"ref","v":"Gn 41:49"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=1Kgs.9.19","r":"1Kgs.9.19","rawR":"1Kgs.9.19","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Kgs.9.19","value":"1Kgs.9.19"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Kgs 9:19"},"). The sons of Jacob traded in Egypt (",{"href":"?bref=Gen.43.11","r":"Gen.43.11","rawR":"Gen.43.11","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Gen.43.11","value":"Gen.43.11"}],"t":"ref","v":"Gn 43:11"},"). In Solomon’s day, trade greatly expanded (",{"href":"?bref=1Kgs.9.26-27","r":"1Kgs.9.26-27","rawR":"1Kgs.9.26-27","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Kgs.9.26-27","value":"1Kgs.9.26-27"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Kgs 9:26-27"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=1Kgs.10.28","r":"1Kgs.10.28","rawR":"1Kgs.10.28","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Kgs.10.28","value":"1Kgs.10.28"}],"t":"ref","v":"10:28"},"). During the exile, Jews became involved in merchant activity in Babylonia, and many never returned to Palestine. In Jerusalem the merchants helped Nehemiah to rebuild the wall (",{"href":"?bref=Neh.3.31-32","r":"Neh.3.31-32","rawR":"Neh.3.31-32","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Neh.3.31-32","value":"Neh.3.31-32"}],"t":"ref","v":"Neh 3:31-32"},")."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"Merchant","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Gn 23:16","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Gen.23.16","rawQueryValue":"Gen.23.16","sourceRefExact":"Gen.23.16"},{"anchorText":"1 Kgs 20:34","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Kgs.20.34","rawQueryValue":"1Kgs.20.34","sourceRefExact":"1Kgs.20.34"},{"anchorText":"Ez 27:16-18","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Ezek.27.16-18","rawQueryValue":"Ezek.27.16-18","sourceRefExact":"Ezek.27.16-18"},{"anchorText":"Is 23:2, 8","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Isa.23.2,8","rawQueryValue":"Isa.23.2,8","sourceRefExact":"Isa.23.2,8"},{"anchorText":"Na 3:16","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Nah.3.16","rawQueryValue":"Nah.3.16","sourceRefExact":"Nah.3.16"},{"anchorText":"Neh 13:16-20","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Neh.13.16-20","rawQueryValue":"Neh.13.16-20","sourceRefExact":"Neh.13.16-20"},{"anchorText":"Ez 27:15, 20-23","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Ezek.27.15,20-23","rawQueryValue":"Ezek.27.15,20-23","sourceRefExact":"Ezek.27.15,20-23"},{"anchorText":"38:13","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Ezek.38.13","rawQueryValue":"Ezek.38.13","sourceRefExact":"Ezek.38.13"},{"anchorText":"1 Kgs 20:34","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Kgs.20.34","rawQueryValue":"1Kgs.20.34","sourceRefExact":"1Kgs.20.34"},{"anchorText":"Neh 3:31","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Neh.3.31","rawQueryValue":"Neh.3.31","sourceRefExact":"Neh.3.31"},{"anchorText":"13:19-20","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Neh.13.19-20","rawQueryValue":"Neh.13.19-20","sourceRefExact":"Neh.13.19-20"},{"anchorText":"Gn 41:49","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Gen.41.49","rawQueryValue":"Gen.41.49","sourceRefExact":"Gen.41.49"},{"anchorText":"1 Kgs 9:19","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Kgs.9.19","rawQueryValue":"1Kgs.9.19","sourceRefExact":"1Kgs.9.19"},{"anchorText":"Gn 43:11","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Gen.43.11","rawQueryValue":"Gen.43.11","sourceRefExact":"Gen.43.11"},{"anchorText":"1 Kgs 9:26-27","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Kgs.9.26-27","rawQueryValue":"1Kgs.9.26-27","sourceRefExact":"1Kgs.9.26-27"},{"anchorText":"10:28","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Kgs.10.28","rawQueryValue":"1Kgs.10.28","sourceRefExact":"1Kgs.10.28"},{"anchorText":"Neh 3:31-32","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Neh.3.31-32","rawQueryValue":"Neh.3.31-32","sourceRefExact":"Neh.3.31-32"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"818c29674e4a01708e8670d3eee0e08389c3b277530ae0b599054c558f04816c","sourceItemName":"Merchant","sourceItemOrder":254,"sourceMember":"Articles/M.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Merchant","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Merchant","title":"Merchant","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}